      "id": "pico-css",
      "kind": "module",
      "title": "Pico CSS",
      "description": "A small CSS kit that makes plain HTML (forms, buttons, tables, cards) look good without writing much CSS.",
      "license": "MIT",
      "source": "https://github.com/picocss/pico",
      "package": "@picocss/pico",
      "version": "2.1.1",
      "howto": "Added as the package @picocss/pico. Load it once in frontend/src/main.tsx with: import '@picocss/pico/css/pico.min.css'; (put it BEFORE the line that imports ./styles.css so your own rules win). Then use plain HTML elements: <main className=\"container\">, <article> for a card, <button>, <input>, <label>, <table>, <nav>. Pico styles those tags directly, so do not add many classes. Use role=\"group\" for button groups and <details> for accordions. Change the accent by overriding the --pico-primary variables in src/styles.css. Do not mix it with another CSS kit.",
      "integrity": "sha512-kIDugA7Ps4U+2BHxiNHmvgPIQDWPDU4IeU6TNRdvXQM1uZX+FibqDQT2xUOnnO2yq/LUHcwnGlu1hvf4KfXnMg==",
