      "howto": "Added as the package motion. In React import from 'motion/react', for example: import { motion } from 'motion/react'; <motion.div initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 8 }} animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }} transition={{ duration: 0.25 }}>...</motion.div>. Keep animations short (under 0.4 seconds) and subtle. Wrap the app or the animated part in <MotionConfig reducedMotion=\"user\"> so people who ask their device for less motion get none. Do not animate everything: use it for appearing content and for state changes.",
