      "source": "written for this platform (docs/AUTH_PLAN.md, docs/SIGN_IN.md)",
      "howto": "Adds Sign in with Google for the visitors of this app, the way the starter has it. Needs a kit of version 2.9.0 or newer (it brings backend/class_auth.py or class_auth.mjs). It adds frontend/src/auth.ts (useUser) and AuthBar.tsx, and a few short edits: in App.tsx the import and <AuthBar /> under the title; in the backend (app.py or index.mjs) the import, class_auth.handle(event) first in the handler, and an example private route /private. If the project's files were changed so the add-on cannot find its place, do it by hand: import class_auth; call class_auth.handle(event) first in the handler and return its answer when there is one; get the visitor with class_auth.current_user(event) or require_user(event); in the page use useUser() from src/auth.ts. Never write a login of your own. Turn it on with npm run signin -- on.",
      "after": "Turn it on with  npm run signin -- on  (it needs your backend on and your teacher's one-time Google setup), then  npm run deploy. On your own computer a pretend visitor signs in at once.",
